From d67c0f37d845a0eaf1d8680ab17111d132b218e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "R. Daneel Olivaw" <rdaneel@gozala.io>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:55:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(query)!: a premise query needs no entity

PremiseQuery::new(premises, select) answers the selected values alone;
.this(variable) adds the entity a variable binds. Rows with none share
one key entity, as an ungrouped fold's do: a premise query is never
restricted to an entity. A selected variable a row leaves unbound is
absent from the row.
---
